From 6ae8c7e9e3772a5a6fdfc4fdc89b03114b60442d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 02:24:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] media: iris: ROG5: SM8350 OEM-firmware platform data
 (secure session, EOS, power off, gating)

The k115 RAM trials on the ROG Phone 5 (SM8350, ASUS vpu20_4v firmware)
established, with the 0157 diagnostics:
- the dummy EOS address 0xdeadb000 makes the firmware take an exception
  (SFR "Exception: ... FA = 0x0", 259 us after that ETB); with a real 4 KiB
  EOS buffer H.264 and HEVC decode bit-exactly, also repeatedly;
- VP9 fails with "CP mode is UNKNOWN" / "CP breached - buffer type 5/6/7"
  (session error 0x1001); stock sends HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_SECURE_SESSION = 0
  for every non-secure session (msm_vdec.c:1205, msm_venc.c:2297) and iris
  never does;
- the generic controller power off asks the CPU NOC at wrapper +0x5c/+0x60,
  which never acknowledges here, and then skips the debug-bridge steps;
  stock Iris2 does X2RPMh, AON MVP NOC and the debug bridge (7, then 0);
- pinned runtime PM with the firmware's power collapse hung the SoC idle;
  disabling the firmware power collapse alone stopped the firmware;
- the H.264 encoder hung the SoC at session start.

Scope all of it to SM8350 through new platform data selected by the
"qcom,sm8350-iris" compatible (the board also lists the qcom,sm8250-venus
fallback, so other SM8250-compatible devices are unchanged):

- SECURE_SESSION = 0 right after SESSION_INIT, before any buffer.
- Real EOS buffer for decoder and encoder drains (no dummy fallback); the
  eos_buffer parameter remains for other gen1 platforms.
- iris_vpu2_sm8350_ops: the stock Iris2 controller power off; handshake
  failures are logged and the first one returned, the power off goes on
  like stock.
- The firmware's inter-frame power collapse stays enabled; the incomplete
  interframe_pc switch of 0161 is removed.
- Opens are refused while runtime PM is pinned (power/control = on); this
  does not guard a later write while the core is up.
- The encoder node is only registered with experimental_encoder=1 and VP9
  only advertised with experimental_vp9=1 (module load time); session open
  refuses both again before SESSION_INIT.
- HFI_PROPERTY_SYS_UBWC_CONFIG with the stock LPDDR5 values (override
  channels/MAL/HBB: 8, 32, 16) after SYS_INIT, stock layout and 60-byte
  size, behind ubwc_config=1 (off by default: decode works without it).

ROG5: patch 0163, kernel k116. Not in upstream.
